I am unable to execute the command to fill in the post details and submit the form due to the missing Chromium distribution. 

You can manually perform the actions in your browser by following these steps:

1. Open the Developer Tools (press `F12` or `Ctrl+Shift+I`).
2. Go to the "Console" tab.
3. Run the following code to fill in the post details:

```javascript
const title = window.postTitle;
const body = window.postBody;
const forum = window.postForum;

document.querySelector('#submission_title').value = title;
document.querySelector('#submission_body').value = body;
document.querySelector('#submission_forum').value = forum;

// To submit the form, you can trigger a click on the submit button
document.querySelector('button.button').click();
```

This will set the title, body, and forum, and then submit the post. If you need further assistance, feel free to ask!
